Cael watches the whole exchange from the gallery above the gate, and the chapter runs his observation discipline at full depth on the one of the four who never speaks: a compact, unhurried woman who spends the entire standoff positioned at the geometric point commanding every exit, laying — he realizes slowly, cataloguing — *nothing*. No declaration, no architecture, no tell. Just placement. The observation notebook gets its first Anchor Path entry that night, built from inference alone: containment craft, fixed-point architecture, the Path that holds people; deployed here as pure positioning, which means discipline of a grade he has seen exactly twice — Seln, and Vastin. Seln confirms the read and adds the fact that matters, in one flat sentence: "Anchor specialists at that grade work enforcement. Enforcement doesn't do assessment escorts. Whoever wrote that paper is done assessing."

