Two firsts, counted on the page even now, because he is who he is: the first notice to say *Silver* — the tier ladder in his log now runs Bronze, Silver, Gold, none of them his. And the first fragment whose source has no name. He reads the notice twice, sitting on the road bank while Brom rights the coach, and writes the entry underneath it that the book has been building toward: "Eight. Taken from someone the system sent namelessly, to hold me namelessly. Every other piece in this log has a person attached — Lira, Feryn, Brom, Reydan, Karis, Seln, Daeva. This one has a hand and no face. I finally own a piece of the machine itself. I don't know yet what that costs. Write it down anyway."

