~4,600 words

The rest chapter — integration cost, aftermath, and the series' third staged birthday, deliberately the smallest and deliberately the last inside an institution's walls. The destabilization is paid on-page per the B3 Ch14 constraint and managed with the B4-established discipline: recovery days banked, the circle warned, nothing evaluable scheduled — and it comes anyway, real: the Anchor-adjacent component *pulls* like nothing before it, wanting to fix points in ordinary rooms, doorways going subtly wrong at the edges of his attention until he learns its idle state; the Storm-adjacent framework, heaviest neighbor, resettles twice. Karis documents the comparative data. Eighth acquisition, second Silver-or-above in two books; her finding, delivered carefully: the architecture is accelerating into heavier sources, and the recovery arithmetic is holding — "for now" entered into the record at her insistence.

