Vastin's moment — the chapter the arc's trust-increments have been buying since Book 4, staged with the discipline the bible's constraint demands: he does not switch sides, and the chapter never once lets him. The approach is the companions' riskiest act of the series and the book prices it on the page: bringing evidence of the falsification to a serving Archmarshal is either the end of the Compact's honest man or the end of the six of them, and they cannot know which until it is done. The mechanics are Seln's — neutral ground in Ostrand, no record, the cache's core exhibits and not the cache itself (tradecraft to the last) — and the vote to do it at all is taken on the page, six hands, unanimous, Seln's raised last and meaning most.

