v3-runs/book-07/packets/ch01-editor-prompt.md:548:    "outcome": "No fight. The shape peels off a hundred meters short of Thornwater's fence-line and is gone the way it came. At the steading's gate the carter, twenty years on this road, says: 'First crew I've hired that knew to shut up.' Cael files the sentence beside the best compliments of his life. Pike's line for the job, arriving by the carter's return, is the chapter's third-party verdict.",
