v3-runs/book-07/packets/ch01-editor-prompt.md:2691:"I made myself the person whose verdict counted, about an event I was never going to be allowed to watch." He said it flatly, with the annoyance of a man who has worked out his own error and does not enjoy it. "So for nine weeks I've been the idiot holding a verdict about a closed session. There is no version of this where I get to deliver the judgment I promised. Whatever I say now is either me pretending I saw something, or me repeating a board."
v3-runs/book-07/packets/ch01-editor-prompt.md:3147:"Hm." It was neither a question nor a verdict. She barred the gate behind him. On the walk above, the man with the bow had already turned back to the road, to the dark where the scrub was, and was looking at it as the carter had looked at the fire: as a fact about the country that did not need his opinion.
